A||N||8||72vinman||The Cost of a new engine???||||5||
Z||000000||72vinman||07-24-2001||08:06 PM||||I am starting to accept the fact that I will probably not find an 86 or 87 GT with A/C in or around the Toronto area for a reasonable price. SO.....There are quite a few 4cyl's for sale. Does anyone know what the cost would be to drop a V8 in an 84 or 85 4cyl car in the Toronto area.<BR>It looks like I can get the car for $1000 or less which would leave me about $3000 left for any mods. Please Help.<BR>72vinman@home.com||||reg||5
Z||000001||Old Lar||07-24-2001||08:16 PM||||If you find the engine the V8 kits for the install are a couple of grand.<P>If you pay someone to do it, it may be $6K.  If you want it done right add a few more to the bottom line.  Like brakes, suspension, transmission, repaint, big stereo system, new wheels, tires.||||reg||1
Z||000002||87FieroGTx||07-24-2001||08:16 PM|||| I think a V8 would cost around 5k for a good job.<P> Why not buy a GT without AC and install a aftermarket AC?<P> You could git a sweet GT for 4k.||||reg||1
Z||000003||72vinman||07-24-2001||08:20 PM||||I talked to the Fiero Shop here in Toronto. He said it is not worth putting the A/C in afterwards. Too much Money and Time. Does anyone else have an opinion on this. I have seen other threads that said it was hard as well. ||||reg||9
Z||000004||LarryB||07-24-2001||10:21 PM||||Talk to them about getting an '85 or later 4 cyl with 5 speed with A/C and having a 3.4 installed.<P><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000005||moonie||07-27-2001||01:26 PM||||<BR>i have a 85se 2.54cyl.<BR>i called American Engine & they quoted me<BR>1,700 for rebuilt 2.5 installed.<BR>i let them take it on a tow truck.<BR>then they called & said it would be 2,200.<BR>i said ok....heck , whats 500 dollars.<BR>then they called back & said it would be 3,000. i said no & to let me come get my car.<BR>well ...it would have been a car without an engine because mine was " supposedly " at the factory.<BR>i wound up paying 3,000 for a rebuilt 2.5 4cyl. <BR>it runs great & has a warranty , but for 3,000 i could have bought a kit from Archie <BR>& put in a 350.<P>my 2 cents.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000006||87ECO5||07-27-2001||02:05 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by LarryB:<BR><B>Talk to them about getting an '85 or later 4 cyl with 5 speed with A/C and having a 3.4 installed.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I had Ed Parks do this "4 to 6" conversion on my '87 4-banger.  Ended up running me over $5000 (American).  Of course, I went with a new (remanufactured) 3.4 and various other stuff (clutch, new gauges, bushing work, exhaust work and various new engine pieces (water pump, belts, hoses, etc.)).<P>Looking at my bill, converting the 4 cylinder car to run with a V6 ran me about $2700 (mostly labor) and the "new" motor was about $1725.<P>If you can do the work yourself, you can probably stay at or under your budget.  I'm not sure if a V8 is the same story.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Old Lar||07-27-2001||02:53 PM||||I'd say about $5k is about right for a new 3.4L engine conversion.  More for other engines with the fun of wiring things together.||||reg||1
Z||000008||RoadRocket||07-27-2001||09:56 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Does anyone know what the cost would be to drop a V8 in an 84 or 85 4cyl car in the Toronto area.<BR>[/B]<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Look here: <A HREF="http://www.v8archie.com/arch10.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.v8archie.com/arch10.htm</A> <P>Overall cost (choosing the modest options) was about 10,000 USD parts & labor.<P>I'm sure, if you do the work yourself, you can cut the costs considerably. But probably not to where you want it.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>||||reg||1
